# Basic Line Plot

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

The simplest line chart: a single `Scatter` trace with x and y arrays.
The default `mode` for `Scatter` is `"lines"` when y values are provided
without an explicit mode.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: [1, 2, 3, 4],
    y: [10, 15, 13, 17]
  )
)
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: [1, 2, 3, 4],
    y: [16, 5, 11, 9]
  )
)
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: [1, 2, 3, 4],
    y: [12, 9, 15, 12]
  )
)
|> Plotly.show()
```
